The goal is to allow the get-kata-rpm step (ci-operator/step-registry/sandboxed-containers-operator/get-kata-rpm) to not
just download and copy the the rpm over the workers but also install (actually upgrade it).

Let me give you the context. That step currently only fetches the rpm file and copies over the workers node, then later
in the workflows that use it there will be another step that will run the openshift-tests-private
(~/src/github.com/openshift/openshift-tests-private) for kata that run some setup routines, including the rpm installation. This is
like that because the rpm only can be installed after the OSC operator is actually installed, and that was the responsability of the
setup routines in openshift-tests-private. It happen that most of those setup routines where moved to a step own itself
(ci-operator/step-registry/sandboxed-containers-operator/install-osc-operator). We will be getting rid of openshift-tests-private soon,
so we are moving its functionalities to other steps.

Given the context, I want to:
* have get-kata-rpm to install the rpm as well, just like the openshift-tests-private does
* get-kata-rpm should be executed after install-osc-operator
* one new feature is to check whether the given rpm version is already installed, otherwise report and do nothing
* the get-kata-rpm name does not make sense anymore. It should be renamed to update-kata-rpm instead

I want to implement that in a couple of commits, grouping the changes logically. For every group of changes (i.e. commits)
you should update the README.md files that references the step as well as the one from the step itself. Commit with -s and add
`Assisted-by: Claude` in the text. Keep the code simple.
